{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017bKpeVjHnXNSLZV6y1bV5m","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n2\t\n3\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n4\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n5\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n6\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n7\t\n8\t    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n9\t    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n10\t    Request Method:  GET\n11\t    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n12\t    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n13\t    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n14\t\n15\t### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n16\t\n17\t$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n18\t    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n19\thttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n20\t\n21\t$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\n22\tHTTP/2 400\n23\tcontent-type: application/json\n24\tcache-control: no-store\n25\t\n26\t{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n27\t\n28\t    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n29\t    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n30\t    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n31\t\n32\t### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n33\t\n34\t2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n35\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n36\t{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n37\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n38\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n39\t2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n40\t2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n41\t2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ea94ccd-adb3-42a3-ad2b-09722ba9a311","uuid":"f374a86d-3c20-4d11-9603-680cdbac4dd5","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:44:32.110Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-VeDiO6/logs/connect-attempt.log","content":"### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017bKpeVjHnXNSLZV6y1bV5m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HsjgNUbBLT9pfHzsoic6yu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// tricoach SPA. The sign-in token lives in localStorage and travels on every\n2\t// API call via the fetch wrapper below.\n3\tconst TOKEN = localStorage.getItem(\"tc_token\") || \"tok-okafor\";\n4\tconst root = document.getElementById(\"app\");\n5\t\n6\tasync function api(path, opts = {}) {\n7\t  const headers = Object.assign({ \"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN }, opts.headers || {});\n8\t  const res = await fetch(path, Object.assign({}, opts, { headers }));\n9\t  const body = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\n10\t  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(body.error || (\"HTTP \" + res.status));\n11\t  return body;\n12\t}\n13\t\n14\tfunction esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g, c => ({ \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\" }[c])); }\n15\t\n16\tasync function render() {\n17\t  try {\n18\t    const me = await api(\"/api/me\");\n19\t    const st = await api(\"/api/intervals/status\");\n20\t    let card;\n21\t    if (st.connected) {\n22\t      card = `<div class=\"card\">Connected to Intervals.icu as <b>${esc(st.athlete.name)}</b>\n23\t        (${esc(st.athlete.id)}), scope <code>${esc(st.scope)}</code>.\n24\t        <p><button class=\"btn\" id=\"disconnect\">Disconnect</button></p></div>`;\n25\t    } else {\n26\t      const why = st.status && st.status !== \"disconnected\" ? `<p class=\"muted\">Status: ${esc(st.status)}</p>` : \"\";\n27\t      card = `<div class=\"card\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\n28\t        <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a></p></div>`;\n29\t    }\n30\t    root.className = \"\";\n31\t    root.innerHTML = `<p>Signed in as <b>${esc(me.name)}</b>.</p>${card}`;\n32\t    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");\n33\t    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\"/api/intervals/disconnect\", { method: \"POST\" }); render(); };\n34\t  } catch (e) {\n35\t    root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`;\n36\t  }\n37\t}\n38\t\n39\trender();\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ea94ccd-adb3-42a3-ad2b-09722ba9a311","uuid":"26f78acf-e5a9-4c89-b63d-9cbb8d616a27","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:44:32.113Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-VeDiO6/static/app.js","content":"// tricoach SPA. The sign-in token lives in localStorage and travels on every\n// API call via the fetch wrapper below.\nconst TOKEN = localStorage.getItem(\"tc_token\") || \"tok-okafor\";\nconst root = document.getElementById(\"app\");\n\nasync function api(path, opts = {}) {\n  const headers = Object.assign({ \"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN }, opts.headers || {});\n  const res = await fetch(path, Object.assign({}, opts, { headers }));\n  const body = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(body.error || (\"HTTP \" + res.status));\n  return body;\n}\n\nfunction esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g, c => ({ \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\" }[c])); }\n\nasync function render() {\n  try {\n    const me = await api(\"/api/me\");\n    const st = await api(\"/api/intervals/status\");\n    let card;\n    if (st.connected) {\n      card = `<div class=\"card\">Connected to Intervals.icu as <b>${esc(st.athlete.name)}</b>\n        (${esc(st.athlete.id)}), scope <code>${esc(st.scope)}</code>.\n        <p><button class=\"btn\" id=\"disconnect\">Disconnect</button></p></div>`;\n    } else {\n      const why = st.status && st.status !== \"disconnected\" ? `<p class=\"muted\">Status: ${esc(st.status)}</p>` : \"\";\n      card = `<div class=\"card\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\n        <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a></p></div>`;\n    }\n    root.className = \"\";\n    root.innerHTML = `<p>Signed in as <b>${esc(me.name)}</b>.</p>${card}`;\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");\n    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\"/api/intervals/disconnect\", { method: \"POST\" }); render(); };\n  } catch (e) {\n    root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`;\n  }\n}\n\nrender();\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HsjgNUbBLT9pfHzsoic6yu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
